Staff Power Electronics Engineer

About Us&nbsp;

Graphcore&nbsp;is a globally recognized leader in Artificial Intelligence computing systems. The company designs advanced semiconductors and data center hardware that provide the specialized processing power needed to drive AI innovation, while delivering the efficiency required to support its broader adoption. &nbsp;&nbsp;

As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies.&nbsp;

Job Overview: &nbsp;

Graphcore is seeking a Senior Engineer, Power Engineering to aid in design, test, and development of the power delivery components from grid to chip. You will work closely with multiple cross-functional teams, including hardware engineers, firmware developers, and data center operations, to ensure the infrastructure we build meets customer requirements as well as attaining standards of performance, reliability, and scalability.&nbsp;

This role will be hybrid-remote, based in Milpitas, CA and will involve a significant in-laboratory component along with some work-from-home.

Responsibilities: &nbsp;

• Contribute to the design and specification of the components and systems in the grid-to-chip power chain.

• Build out the test environment and perform engineering test and validation of the grid-to-chip chain.

• Design test hardware including the overall test environment, test fixtures, loads, and other devices to simulate various loading conditions and to evaluate the performance of the power chain.&nbsp; Testing includes basic function testing, robustness and reliability testing, high-power cycle testing, high-bandwidth power testing, energy storage testing, and numerous other types of tests involved in AI power system validation.

• Design and prototype custom components as may be needed to support the Graphcore power architecture.&nbsp; This includes the low-level design of power conversion hardware and rapid prototyping.&nbsp;

• Support the transition of system designs from test and validation into the manufacturing and production environments

• Ensure robustness of IT power in the presence of grid disturbances and make sure that IT power loads are compatible with grid power requirements (“good grid power citizen”)&nbsp;

• Provide guidance to the power equipment manufacturers, ODM and engineering teams on the required testing and validation procedures for power hardware and firmware components.&nbsp;

• Tackle and resolve sophisticated power hardware and firmware issues as needed.&nbsp;

Required Skills and&nbsp;Experience : &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s or&nbsp;Master’s&nbsp;or PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, &nbsp;knowledge of Power Electronics desired.

• Demonstrated ability in power system and delivery architecture, design, and development.&nbsp;

• Experience testing high voltage and high power systems, Proficiency&nbsp;in power hardware and firmware development and debugging.&nbsp;

• Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills.&nbsp;

• Strong communication&nbsp;and teamwork skills.&nbsp;

• Ability to work in a fast-paced, multifaceted environment.&nbsp;

"Nice to Have" Skills and Experience: &nbsp;

• Familiarity with new technologies in AI and data center infrastructure.&nbsp;

Benefits&nbsp; &nbsp;
&nbsp;
In addition to a competitive salary,&nbsp;Graphcore&nbsp;offers a competitive benefits package. We welcome people of&nbsp;different backgrounds&nbsp;and experiences;&nbsp;we’re&nbsp;committed to building an inclusive work environment that makes&nbsp;Graphcore&nbsp;a great home&nbsp;for everyone. We offer an equal opportunity process and understand that there are visible and invisible differences in all of us. We can provide a flexible approach to interview and encourage you to chat to us if you&nbsp;require&nbsp;any reasonable adjustments. &nbsp;

Intrinsic is an AI robotics group at Google aiming to reimagine the potential of industrial robotics. Our team believes that advances in AI, perception and simulation will redefine what’s possible for industrial robotics in the near future - with software and data at the core.

Our mission is to make industrial robotics intelligent, accessible, and usable for millions more businesses, entrepreneurs, and developers. We are a dynamic team of engineers, roboticists, designers, and technologists who are passionate about unlocking the creative and economic potential of industrial robotics.

Role

As a Full Stack Senior Software Engineer in our Product Development Team for Robotic Solutions you will work closely together with different stakeholders to develop production ready software for scalable robot applications based on our Intrinsic Platform. You will be part of the entire development journey, from scoping the right technical solution, analyzing dependencies and needs up to actual development and testing.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

How your work moves the mission forward

• Synchronize with product management and platform development to take the right architecture decisions, which ensure long term maintainability and stability.&nbsp;

• Implement high quality software with state of the art tooling as part of an experienced team of developers.

• Be hands on in testing on real hardware and supporting customers where needed.

• Ensure a smooth transition of feature releases to the Customer Success Team, which will take care of most customer facing enablement and support.&nbsp;

